WEBVTT

00:00:25.362 --> 00:00:29.065
Eirene is coming down...

00:00:29.065 --> 00:00:30.633
...to wipe out this city.

00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:32.669
Eirene?

00:00:32.669 --> 00:00:37.674
Like Eunomia, one of the three
colonization control computers.

00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:41.878
It's also the core computer
of our colony ship.

00:00:41.878 --> 00:00:47.317
It must've been observing the city
for 200 years from the skies.

00:00:47.317 --> 00:00:48.852
From the skies?

00:00:48.852 --> 00:00:52.185
That colonization ship is going
to crash down on the city?

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:54.024
Yes.

00:00:54.024 --> 00:00:55.392
Wait a minute!

00:00:55.392 --> 00:00:57.627
You just said there were three, right?

00:00:57.627 --> 00:01:00.663
One was Eunomia,
the second is this Eirene...

00:01:00.663 --> 00:01:03.133
Then, what of the remaining one?

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:04.896
It's...

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:09.739
Not... Solty?!

00:01:09.739 --> 00:01:10.707
What?!

00:01:10.707 --> 00:01:12.265
I don't believe it!

00:01:14.511 --> 00:01:18.815
Eirene wants to wipe out
everyone in this city.

00:01:18.815 --> 00:01:19.749
What?

00:01:19.749 --> 00:01:22.552
And she wants to rewrite human history.

00:01:22.552 --> 00:01:24.320
That's awful...

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.222
I will go up into the sky and stop Eirene.

00:01:29.225 --> 00:01:32.595
The estimated time of tomorrow's
colony ship crash has been released.

00:01:32.595 --> 00:01:34.030
Tomorrow...

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:36.599
The estimated time is 20:56.

00:01:36.599 --> 00:01:39.069
- You have not finished your meal yet!
- Old man!

00:01:39.069 --> 00:01:42.939
- I'm going out.
- Currently, the RUC's
security department is helping.

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:45.931
- Solty...
- to evacuate citizens
to the underground city...

00:01:47.277 --> 00:01:47.577
Don't panic!

00:01:47.577 --> 00:01:48.578
"From Here On Out"
Don't panic!

00:01:48.578 --> 00:01:50.046
"From Here On Out"
Please don't push!

00:01:50.046 --> 00:01:51.980
"From Here On Out"

00:01:53.049 --> 00:01:56.419
There's still plenty of space
in the underground city.

00:01:56.419 --> 00:02:01.379
Please get your food and water at
the tents set up at various locations.

00:02:02.791 --> 00:02:06.161
So the city's entire population is
evacuating to the underground city.

00:02:06.161 --> 00:02:09.231
But if the colony ship
does come crashing down,

00:02:09.231 --> 00:02:11.600
this place won't be safe either, right?

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.134
Seems that way.

00:02:13.134 --> 00:02:14.970
They had it on the news:

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:18.306
RUC's engineers are said to be
working with the private sector

00:02:18.306 --> 00:02:22.436
on a plan to blow up the colony ship
before it comes crashing down.

00:02:30.785 --> 00:02:33.922
Everybody's gone...

00:02:33.922 --> 00:02:36.725
So much for business.

00:02:36.725 --> 00:02:40.562
So, why're you here?

00:02:40.562 --> 00:02:44.866
I just had a feeling you'd be here.

00:02:44.866 --> 00:02:46.468
I see.

00:02:46.468 --> 00:02:49.237
Why're you here, Mister?

00:02:49.237 --> 00:02:54.376
I just had a feeling you'd come here.

00:02:54.376 --> 00:02:56.478
Oh.

00:02:56.478 --> 00:02:58.980
Shouldn't you be evacuating underground?

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.849
Your family must be worried about you.

00:03:00.849 --> 00:03:04.986
I'm fine here.
Besides, I don't have a family.

00:03:04.986 --> 00:03:06.721
I see.

00:03:06.721 --> 00:03:08.023
How about you, Mister?

00:03:08.023 --> 00:03:11.326
Dead. Both my wife and my kids.

00:03:11.326 --> 00:03:13.461
Twelve years ago.

00:03:13.461 --> 00:03:15.730
Oh.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.799
Say...

00:03:17.799 --> 00:03:20.535
lf... Just saying "if"...

00:03:20.535 --> 00:03:22.935
If we survive...

00:03:24.172 --> 00:03:25.935
Would you...

00:03:27.342 --> 00:03:29.778
Sarah...

00:03:29.778 --> 00:03:31.575
I...

00:03:34.282 --> 00:03:36.451
We are going to use this?

00:03:36.451 --> 00:03:40.055
Yes. It's the machine Ashley built.

00:03:40.055 --> 00:03:42.257
It was broken in many places,

00:03:42.257 --> 00:03:44.993
but fortunately,
the main section was functional.

00:03:44.993 --> 00:03:48.530
Right now, the RUC is devoting
all of its resources to repairing it.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:51.166
We'll send you up into the sky in this.

00:03:51.166 --> 00:03:53.034
Okay.

00:03:53.034 --> 00:03:54.803
I'm sorry...

00:03:54.803 --> 00:03:57.772
In the end, we have to depend on you.

00:03:57.772 --> 00:03:59.741
Please do not let it bother you.

00:03:59.741 --> 00:04:04.872
Rather, I should be thanking you
for preparing all of this for me.

00:04:08.016 --> 00:04:10.246
Solty!

00:04:11.987 --> 00:04:14.422
Are you truly all right with this?

00:04:14.422 --> 00:04:17.692
Your chances of coming back
are just about nil.

00:04:17.692 --> 00:04:19.928
Do you still insist on...

00:04:19.928 --> 00:04:21.555
Mr. Joseph...

00:04:24.332 --> 00:04:27.202
When we were up in space,
when you were still known as Dike...

00:04:27.202 --> 00:04:29.337
To be frank, you made me
feel uncomfortable.

00:04:29.337 --> 00:04:31.973
You were mechanical,
and struck me as cold.

00:04:31.973 --> 00:04:34.909
I even felt afraid of you.

00:04:34.909 --> 00:04:38.046
But now, you have a wonderful smile.

00:04:38.046 --> 00:04:39.843
Is it thanks to Roy?

00:04:43.718 --> 00:04:46.588
Oh, are you all by yourself, Solty?

00:04:46.588 --> 00:04:51.026
Mr. Roy stepped out, and Miss Rose
said she did not have an appetite.

00:04:51.026 --> 00:04:52.627
That's too bad...

00:04:52.627 --> 00:04:56.231
This was supposed to be
a dinner party for you.

00:04:56.231 --> 00:04:58.666
What do you think? Did it turn out good?

00:04:58.666 --> 00:05:03.238
Yes! Just what I would expect
from my cooking teacher!

00:05:03.238 --> 00:05:04.873
Thank you.

00:05:04.873 --> 00:05:07.742
It'll almost be a year
since you first came...

00:05:07.742 --> 00:05:09.444
Oh, is that so?

00:05:09.444 --> 00:05:10.412
That's right.

00:05:10.412 --> 00:05:15.116
I know! We have to throw you
a birthday party!

00:05:15.116 --> 00:05:18.420
Oh... But you don't know
when your birthday is, do you?

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.521
Um...

00:05:19.521 --> 00:05:22.791
I believe it is June 30th by your calendar.

00:05:22.791 --> 00:05:25.060
My! That's pretty close.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:26.494
How old will you be?

00:05:26.494 --> 00:05:30.098
That... is a bit embarrassing,
so it is a secret.

00:05:30.098 --> 00:05:31.032
Oh?

00:05:31.032 --> 00:05:32.901
Let's invite everyone to the party, okay?

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:34.198
Okay!

00:05:35.336 --> 00:05:38.473
What's the matter?
You haven't eaten much.

00:05:38.473 --> 00:05:40.742
It is delicious, you know.

00:05:40.742 --> 00:05:42.844
- Solty...
- Yes?

00:05:42.844 --> 00:05:45.747
You will come back, won't you?

00:05:45.747 --> 00:05:48.950
Kasha...

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.785
Solty?

00:05:50.785 --> 00:05:52.520
Give me an answer!

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:55.457
I know you have to go.

00:05:55.457 --> 00:05:58.827
But there's a chance
you might not come back...

00:05:58.827 --> 00:06:04.060
If you don't go, this thing will
fall down on us and we'll all die...

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.103
I don't want to die, either...

00:06:08.103 --> 00:06:12.199
But I don't want you to go!

00:06:14.309 --> 00:06:16.072
Kasha...

00:06:29.757 --> 00:06:31.860
So you were back.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.158
What're you doing up here?

00:06:38.967 --> 00:06:40.702
You're incredible, Roy.

00:06:40.702 --> 00:06:42.504
Huh?

00:06:42.504 --> 00:06:43.638
Incredible.

00:06:43.638 --> 00:06:46.074
What part of me?

00:06:46.074 --> 00:06:48.977
Do you remember when I first met Kasha?

00:06:48.977 --> 00:06:50.535
Yeah.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:56.618
She wouldn't take to me at all.

00:06:56.618 --> 00:06:58.586
Yeah, I remember.

00:06:58.586 --> 00:07:02.624
It took two years before
she began calling me Mom.

00:07:02.624 --> 00:07:08.129
But you became family
with Solty in less than a year.

00:07:08.129 --> 00:07:10.865
That's why you're incredible.

00:07:10.865 --> 00:07:13.868
Why're you running from Solty?

00:07:13.868 --> 00:07:16.530
You should be spending time with her.

00:07:21.643 --> 00:07:27.916
She was nothing but
a nuisance to me at first.

00:07:27.916 --> 00:07:31.147
She appeared out of nowhere
and messed up my life.

00:07:32.754 --> 00:07:37.225
But before I knew it, she was family.

00:07:37.225 --> 00:07:38.626
Yes.

00:07:38.626 --> 00:07:43.231
If she doesn't go tomorrow,
all of us here will die.

00:07:43.231 --> 00:07:44.065
Yes.

00:07:44.065 --> 00:07:47.001
Me, you, Rose, Kasha...

00:07:47.001 --> 00:07:48.736
...the others... Everyone!

00:07:48.736 --> 00:07:53.808
I have to make her shoulder the burden
of everyone's fate all alone!

00:07:53.808 --> 00:07:55.944
Is that what hurts?

00:07:55.944 --> 00:08:00.014
Going to see her would mean I consent

00:08:00.014 --> 00:08:03.251
to sending her away to a place
from where she might not return.

00:08:03.251 --> 00:08:05.053
Is that why you won't see her?

00:08:05.053 --> 00:08:08.423
I... I...

00:08:08.423 --> 00:08:12.291
Why do they all leave me?!

00:08:14.429 --> 00:08:16.192
Roy...

00:08:20.101 --> 00:08:22.160
Why?

00:08:34.649 --> 00:08:36.378
Thank you for waiting for me.

00:08:37.719 --> 00:08:39.687
It looks pretty sharp on you.

00:08:39.687 --> 00:08:41.356
Thank you very much.

00:08:41.356 --> 00:08:44.259
I will be borrowing your suit, Miss Rose.

00:08:44.259 --> 00:08:46.527
Don't mention it.

00:08:46.527 --> 00:08:48.763
We've done all that we can.

00:08:48.763 --> 00:08:50.331
The rest is up to you.

00:08:50.331 --> 00:08:51.532
I know.

00:08:51.532 --> 00:08:53.735
Solty...

00:08:53.735 --> 00:08:54.869
What?

00:08:54.869 --> 00:08:56.337
Let's shake hands.

00:08:56.337 --> 00:08:58.906
We've never properly done it.

00:08:58.906 --> 00:09:02.277
This time, I'll realize
my ideals my own way.

00:09:02.277 --> 00:09:05.813
So go out there and protect our future.

00:09:05.813 --> 00:09:08.316
Miss Rose...

00:09:08.316 --> 00:09:09.450
I will!

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:13.254
You're a part of my ideal.
Remember that.

00:09:13.254 --> 00:09:15.723
Make sure you come back!

00:09:15.723 --> 00:09:17.992
All right. I understand.

00:09:17.992 --> 00:09:19.193
Solty.

00:09:19.193 --> 00:09:22.730
Oh, Ms. Miranda... Kasha...

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:24.699
Be careful out there, okay?

00:09:24.699 --> 00:09:25.900
I will.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.469
Kasha...

00:09:28.469 --> 00:09:30.638
Kasha...

00:09:30.638 --> 00:09:32.907
When you come back...

00:09:32.907 --> 00:09:34.742
When you come back,

00:09:34.742 --> 00:09:37.643
I'm kicking you in the butt!

00:09:42.283 --> 00:09:44.118
Then I'll forgive you.

00:09:44.118 --> 00:09:46.854
Please do not make it hurt too much, okay?

00:09:46.854 --> 00:09:47.922
No can do.

00:09:47.922 --> 00:09:51.059
You sure you don't have to
say something to her, too?

00:09:51.059 --> 00:09:52.293
I'm sure.

00:09:52.293 --> 00:09:54.629
- Solty will come back for sure.
- No way!
- But...

00:09:54.629 --> 00:09:54.996
- So, I don't have to do it now.
- No means no!

00:09:54.996 --> 00:09:57.332
- So, I don't have to do it now.
- No means no!

00:09:57.332 --> 00:10:01.102
Hey! You say that now, but later on...

00:10:01.102 --> 00:10:03.570
Damn you for trying to act cool!

00:10:04.939 --> 00:10:07.075
It's almost time...

00:10:07.075 --> 00:10:08.474
Right!

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:17.645
Solty...

00:10:21.956 --> 00:10:24.192
- I will be going now.
- Hold it!

00:10:24.192 --> 00:10:25.352
Oh...

00:10:30.098 --> 00:10:31.588
Mr. Roy...

00:10:43.344 --> 00:10:46.814
You're late! What were you
doing all this time?!

00:10:46.814 --> 00:10:48.416
Huh?

00:10:48.416 --> 00:10:51.686
Mr. Roy, um, I am going
to board this now and...

00:10:51.686 --> 00:10:53.421
- Don't go!
- What?

00:10:53.421 --> 00:10:55.256
Don't go out into space!

00:10:55.256 --> 00:10:56.357
Stay here!

00:10:56.357 --> 00:10:58.459
- Roy!
- Shut up!

00:10:58.459 --> 00:11:04.065
If you fail to destroy the colony ship,
everyone here will die!

00:11:04.065 --> 00:11:06.934
Even if you succeed,
if a fragment falls on the city,

00:11:06.934 --> 00:11:10.505
they say the result will still be the same!

00:11:10.505 --> 00:11:11.539
Yes.

00:11:11.539 --> 00:11:13.408
Then stay right here!

00:11:13.408 --> 00:11:17.345
If it's the same whether you go or not,
it's better to stay here!

00:11:17.345 --> 00:11:20.081
I know! Let's go on a drive!

00:11:20.081 --> 00:11:22.049
Or would you prefer the amusement park?

00:11:22.049 --> 00:11:25.119
We haven't been to one yet, right?
It's a lot of fun!

00:11:25.119 --> 00:11:27.155
- We'll take your
homemade lunches with us!
- Roy...

00:11:27.155 --> 00:11:29.323
- That's what we'll do!
- Old man...

00:11:29.323 --> 00:11:31.926
Come on, let's go home.

00:11:31.926 --> 00:11:36.397
I am sorry. I cannot do that.

00:11:36.397 --> 00:11:37.498
Why not?

00:11:37.498 --> 00:11:40.501
I want to protect you and the others.

00:11:40.501 --> 00:11:43.504
Why does it have to be you?

00:11:43.504 --> 00:11:47.241
I am happy to be able to protect everyone.

00:11:47.241 --> 00:11:48.376
I've heard enough!

00:11:48.376 --> 00:11:49.911
You don't have to go!

00:11:49.911 --> 00:11:51.379
Don't go!

00:11:51.379 --> 00:11:52.447
I...

00:11:52.447 --> 00:11:54.916
I'm telling you not to go!

00:11:54.916 --> 00:11:55.983
Mr. Roy...

00:11:55.983 --> 00:11:58.519
If you're my daughter,
do as your father says!

00:11:58.519 --> 00:11:59.884
What?

00:12:04.525 --> 00:12:06.254
Damn it!

00:12:11.699 --> 00:12:13.301
You have made me so happy.

00:12:13.301 --> 00:12:16.370
I am a machine, and yet...

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:19.040
You called me your daughter.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:20.875
I am so happy!

00:12:20.875 --> 00:12:25.505
What more can I say?

00:12:27.148 --> 00:12:31.719
Mr. Roy, I love you very much.

00:12:31.719 --> 00:12:33.421
That is why...

00:12:33.421 --> 00:12:35.082
I am going.

00:12:40.261 --> 00:12:42.463
Solty...

00:12:42.463 --> 00:12:44.294
Solty!

00:12:49.403 --> 00:12:51.105
She's gone.

00:12:51.105 --> 00:12:54.141
Now all we can do...

00:12:54.141 --> 00:12:56.277
...is pray.

00:12:56.277 --> 00:13:00.213
Come, we'd better hurry
and take shelter underground as well.

00:13:02.917 --> 00:13:06.182
I'm fine where I am.

00:13:27.408 --> 00:13:30.344
Dike, so it was you.

00:13:30.344 --> 00:13:32.847
You shot at me knowing that, did you not?

00:13:32.847 --> 00:13:35.716
Why would I shoot you?

00:13:35.716 --> 00:13:37.451
Please do not play dumb!

00:13:37.451 --> 00:13:42.354
It appears that you,
like Eunomia, have gone out of control.

00:13:46.027 --> 00:13:47.295
One year ago,

00:13:47.295 --> 00:13:49.830
we became aware that
Eunomia was out of control,

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:52.266
so I went down to the surface.

00:13:52.266 --> 00:13:55.770
But Eunomia was not the only one
that had gone out of control.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:59.240
After I went down, you also...

00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:04.145
I have a mission: Never allow
the species of man to perish.

00:14:04.145 --> 00:14:06.477
If you intend to interfere
with that mission...

00:14:08.783 --> 00:14:14.488
We shot down the people who tried
to return from the surface.

00:14:14.488 --> 00:14:18.359
Your laser fire was dispersed by
the shell surrounding the atmosphere,

00:14:18.359 --> 00:14:20.861
placing excessive electrical loads
on the nanomachines,

00:14:20.861 --> 00:14:24.599
causing the lightning bolt phenomena
from the Aurora Shell.

00:14:24.599 --> 00:14:28.202
And that was also what caused Blast Fall.

00:14:28.202 --> 00:14:32.006
I did it to protect the
people on the surface.

00:14:32.006 --> 00:14:33.140
Two hundred years ago,

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:38.312
we had no way to stop the epidemic
that spread through the colony ship.

00:14:38.312 --> 00:14:41.782
You collected the DNA patterns
from the people as they died

00:14:41.782 --> 00:14:42.950
and converted them to data.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:45.519
It is a valuable record
of the species of man.

00:14:45.519 --> 00:14:47.555
As long as we have the data I hold,

00:14:47.555 --> 00:14:51.058
we can recreate the
history of man at any time.

00:14:51.058 --> 00:14:53.185
Human beings are not data!

00:14:57.832 --> 00:15:01.035
They have emotions
and live life to the fullest.

00:15:01.035 --> 00:15:04.005
They do so now and
they will continue to do so!

00:15:04.005 --> 00:15:09.677
Those very emotions gave rise to people
who threatened my existence.

00:15:09.677 --> 00:15:13.014
Humans are creatures who willingly
choose a path to destruction.

00:15:13.014 --> 00:15:18.552
That is why I manage them as data,
the most efficient method.

00:15:18.552 --> 00:15:21.622
Those are not human beings!
That is only data!

00:15:21.622 --> 00:15:26.794
No, humans will continue to live
together with me, for all time.

00:15:26.794 --> 00:15:30.286
And for that, you would destroy that city?!

00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:36.137
I do it so I can go on
forever with mankind.

00:15:36.137 --> 00:15:37.938
What you are doing is wrong!

00:15:37.938 --> 00:15:39.997
Why will you not understand?

00:15:40.975 --> 00:15:43.944
Let us end this, Eirene.

00:16:01.595 --> 00:16:05.463
Is it your intention to destroy me, Dike?

00:16:06.667 --> 00:16:09.770
The three of us are a single entity.

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:13.140
You could say I am your alter ego.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:16.410
Are you going to destroy me?

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:19.714
To protect those dear to me...

00:16:19.714 --> 00:16:22.012
You cannot protect man.

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:32.893
Maybe so...

00:16:32.893 --> 00:16:35.691
You cannot become human.

00:16:40.701 --> 00:16:42.269
Perhaps...

00:16:42.269 --> 00:16:47.536
But there are people who are
waiting for me to return.

00:16:49.176 --> 00:16:53.545
Even someone who calls me his daughter...

00:16:54.949 --> 00:16:55.883
Dike!

00:16:55.883 --> 00:16:58.750
I am Solty Revant!

00:17:04.825 --> 00:17:05.985
Stop!

00:17:31.786 --> 00:17:33.777
So many falling stars!

00:17:41.929 --> 00:17:44.022
It's beautiful...

00:17:47.401 --> 00:17:50.004
Dad! Hurry, hurry!

00:17:50.004 --> 00:17:50.271
H-Hey, wait for me.

00:17:50.271 --> 00:17:52.973
H-Hey, wait for me.

00:17:52.973 --> 00:17:56.143
You're not going to
lose your belly like that!

00:17:56.143 --> 00:18:00.281
Come on, we're grocers,
so we can't sell belly.

00:18:00.281 --> 00:18:01.976
H-Hey!

00:18:03.417 --> 00:18:06.187
Today, with the privatization
of the RUC's resemble plants,

00:18:06.187 --> 00:18:08.289
the final step has been taken
in the complete dismantling

00:18:08.289 --> 00:18:11.225
of the commercial, judicial,
and government systems

00:18:11.225 --> 00:18:13.060
managed by the RUC.

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:14.295
- I guess it's already been five years.
- Now for our next story.

00:18:14.295 --> 00:18:16.730
- I guess it's already been five years.
- We now have our youngest
female assemblywoman ever.

00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:19.500
- Wasn't your name Rose Anderson?
- Representative Rita Revant said
she will focus on problems that remain

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.869
- Wasn't your name Rose Anderson?
- Even after the abolishment of
the resident registration system...

00:18:21.869 --> 00:18:27.908
Well, I couldn't very well run
in an election as "Thief Rose".

00:18:27.908 --> 00:18:30.711
I'm the daughter you're
so proud of. Right, Dad?

00:18:30.711 --> 00:18:34.782
Yeah, I'm very proud of my daughters...

00:18:34.782 --> 00:18:37.952
Both you and her.

00:18:37.952 --> 00:18:39.753
You're still waiting?

00:18:39.753 --> 00:18:42.156
Yeah.

00:18:42.156 --> 00:18:44.491
I am, too, actually.

00:18:44.491 --> 00:18:47.661
I waited twelve years for you.

00:18:47.661 --> 00:18:49.763
It's only been five years.

00:18:49.763 --> 00:18:50.364
Yes.

00:18:50.364 --> 00:18:52.833
You see, I knew they'd be together!

00:18:52.833 --> 00:18:55.870
Rose! Quit slacking!

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:57.838
Give me back my radio!

00:18:57.838 --> 00:18:58.839
Uh-oh...

00:18:58.839 --> 00:19:01.273
Your capable secretary has arrived.

00:19:03.878 --> 00:19:08.015
Not to worry. Solty will come back.

00:19:08.015 --> 00:19:12.152
After all, her family
is waiting for her here.

00:19:12.152 --> 00:19:13.813
Yes.

00:19:23.596 --> 00:19:26.966
Cover up my tears

00:19:26.966 --> 00:19:31.370
Let me cover up my tears

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:35.741
In the pieces

00:19:35.741 --> 00:19:41.313
In the pieces

00:19:41.313 --> 00:19:50.089
If you need me, I'll sit next to you

00:19:50.089 --> 00:19:58.831
Playing piano all night

00:19:58.831 --> 00:20:19.549
Soaking up every last note of music
spun by those hands

00:20:50.616 --> 00:20:51.183
Roy. Roy?

00:20:51.183 --> 00:20:53.219
Roy. Roy?

00:20:53.219 --> 00:20:54.587
Roy, do you read me?

00:20:54.587 --> 00:20:57.523
Yeah, I read you.

00:20:57.523 --> 00:21:01.894
With this much debris,
it won't be easy to find her.

00:21:01.894 --> 00:21:05.598
Let's go back and run a
scan of the area once more.

00:21:05.598 --> 00:21:08.300
You're sure it's around here, right?

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:12.171
Yes, I ran the calculations many times.

00:21:12.171 --> 00:21:16.475
I still have oxygen. You go on back ahead.

00:21:16.475 --> 00:21:18.102
Roy...

00:21:19.645 --> 00:21:22.248
What's that sound?

00:21:22.248 --> 00:21:24.016
Is that...

00:21:24.016 --> 00:21:26.752
...a tune?

00:21:26.752 --> 00:21:28.515
This tune is...

00:21:38.297 --> 00:21:39.632
You foolish girl!

00:21:39.632 --> 00:21:41.567
Wandering down a broken road
You foolish girl!

00:21:41.567 --> 00:21:46.372
Wandering down a broken road
You were so late, I came to get you.

00:21:46.372 --> 00:21:48.674
Even should this journey continue

00:21:48.674 --> 00:21:51.577
Even should this journey continue
Solty!

00:21:51.577 --> 00:21:52.878
Even should this journey continue
Welcome home!

00:21:52.878 --> 00:21:58.214
Someday, you will arrive

00:22:00.586 --> 00:22:05.591
At your home sweet home

00:22:05.591 --> 00:22:07.459
Come, wipe your tears
I...

00:22:07.459 --> 00:22:08.961
Come, wipe your tears
...am...

00:22:08.961 --> 00:22:10.462
Come, wipe your tears
...ho...

00:22:10.462 --> 00:22:11.930
Come, wipe your tears
...me...

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:18.370
Don't cry anymore

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:27.646
Give your loved ones a kiss now

00:22:27.646 --> 00:22:34.245
So that you may
see them again tomorrow

00:22:37.256 --> 00:22:43.929
Where do stars that have fallen go?

00:22:43.929 --> 00:22:50.369
Where are they guided to?

00:22:50.369 --> 00:23:02.304
That is my guidepost, my one and only
